{%- comment -%}
  One active-filter pill - the whole <facet-remove> element.

  Accepts: filter (required), value (required)

  This markup was written out four times in snippets/facets.liquid (the drawer, the two
  desktop layouts and the mobile sheet), identical in all four but for indentation, each
  preceded by the same two lines of label plumbing. Four copies of a control whose job is
  "let the visitor undo a filter" is four chances for one of them to stop undoing it.

  The label comes from lena-color-facet with `fallback: 'clean'`. A pill must never be
  hidden: it is the only control that removes the filter, so hiding it would strand a
  visitor with a filter applied and no way to clear it. 'clean' therefore tidies a
  non-whitelisted value - "color-accessories" prints as "Accessories" - instead of dropping
  it. The checkbox lists pass no fallback and still hide such values, which is right for a
  list you choose from.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- capture fp_raw -%}
  {%- render 'lena-color-facet', filter: filter, value: value, fallback: 'clean' -%}
{%- endcapture -%}
{%- assign fp_label = fp_raw | strip -%}
<facet-remove>
  <a href="{{ value.url_to_remove }}" class="active-facets__button active-facets__button--light">
    <span class="active-facets__button-inner button button--tertiary">
      {{ filter.label | escape }}: {{ fp_label | escape }}
      <span class="svg-wrapper">
        {{- 'icon-close-small.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}
      </span>
      <span class="visually-hidden">{{ 'products.facets.clear_filter' | t }}</span>
    </span>
  </a>
</facet-remove>
